### User-defined functions

New functions may be defined<sup>1.49.0</sup>:

```just
set unstable

hello(name) := f"Hello, {{ name }}!"

foo:
  echo '{{ hello("World") }}'
```

User-defined functions are currently unstable.

Functions may reference assignments in the same module:

```just
set unstable

base := "foo"

join(extension) := base + "." + extension

create:
  touch {{ join("c") }}
  touch {{ join("html") }}
  touch {{ join("txt") }}
```

### Constants

A number of constants are predefined:
use super::*;

#[test]
fn bugfix() {
  let mut justfile = String::from("foo: (x ");
  for _ in 0..500 {
    justfile.push('(');
  }
  Test::new()
    .justfile(&justfile)
    .stderr(RECURSION_LIMIT_REACHED)
    .failure();
}

const RECURSION_LIMIT_REACHED: &str = if cfg!(windows) {
  "
error: Parsing recursion depth exceeded
